Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:46:16 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Step 8: search across all documents + one-line summaries

- search_index.py: page-aware chunking, OpenAI-compatible embeddings
  (e.g. bge-m3 on vLLM), Postgres+pgvector store (HNSW + full-text) or local
  SQLite fallback, hybrid ranking (vector + Arabic-stemmed keywords, RRF)
- search_documents tool: best passages from ALL the user's files with
  doc_id + page; per-user isolation; results fenced as untrusted
- find_in_document: doc_id "all" searches every file; Arabic-tolerant
  matching (diacritics, alef forms, ya/ta marbuta, Arabic digits) that
  returns the original wording
- One-line summary per file (housekeeping model) in AVAILABLE DOCUMENTS
- Automatic incremental indexing per turn, /reindex, CLI with --force
- Grounding and tool-activity notes understand search_documents
- Load .env before local modules read their settings
- tests/test_step8.py (runs on SQLite or pgvector)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
